[187.880639, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The fireball, half of it white, half azure blue, and the size of a ten inch shell, moved slowly about the raft,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  but revolving on its own axis with astonishing velocity, as if whipped round by the force of the whirlwind.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The bond of union thus effected could never be severed, and although Ben Zuf's achievements had fairly earned\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  him the right of retirement, he firmly declined all honours or any pension that might part him from his superior\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  officer.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Before the settlement of terms the administration must be possessed entirely by the parliaments of both\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  kingdoms, and how incompatible that scheme with the liberty of the king is easily imagined.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The London plant was less temporary, but not permanent, supplying, before it was torn out, no fewer than three\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  thousand lamps in hotels, churches, stores, and dwellings in the vicinity of Holborn Viaduct.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  It may be that a great colourist will use his utmost force of colour, as a singer his full power of voice, but,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  loud or low, the virtue is in both cases always in refinement, never in loudness.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  He doesn't say, but it's on the frontier, and on the map, everything beyond it is marked Indians and desert, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  looks as desolate as a Wednesday meeting. Humph. It was time for him to do something.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  a large open fireplace with rusty dogs in it, and a bare boarded floor. At the far end fleeces of wool stacked\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  up. In the middle of the floor some empty corn bags.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Much later, when a friend of his was preparing an edition of all his Latin works, he remarked to his home\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  circle, If I had my way about it, they would republish only those of my books which have doctrine my Galatians,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  for instance,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  It was the white rabbit returning, splendidly dressed with a pair of white kid gloves in one hand and a large\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  fan in the other. He came trotting along in a great hurry, muttering to himself as he came Oh, the Duchess, the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Duchess\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The dependent who was first delegated for these duties was the wife, or the chief wife, and, as would be\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  expected, in the later development of the institution, when the number of persons by whom these duties are\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  customarily performed gradually narrows, the wife remains the last.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Shall I never miss home talk, and blessing, and the common kiss that comes to each in turn, Nor count it\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  strange, when I look up, To drop on a new range of walls and floors, another home than this?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  It is also noticeable that the serviceability of consumption as a means of repute, as well as the insistence on\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  it as an element of decency, is at its best in those portions of the community where the human contact of the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  individual is widest and the mobility of the population is greatest.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Assuredly, if the tongue which a nation or a province has spoken is worthy of interest, the language which has\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  been spoken by a misery is still more worthy of attention and study.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  We don't spin tops, is a favourite saying amongst artillery officers, indicating that they do not shirk their\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  duty by frivolous pursuits. But it must be confessed that Cervadac, being naturally idle, was very much given to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  spinning tops.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  I have not asked him, Ruth replied, with a look that might imply that she was one of those determined little\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  bodies who first made up her own mind and then compelled others to make up theirs in accordance with hers.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The strong position held by the Edison system under the strenuous competition that was already springing up was\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  enormously improved by the introduction of the three wire system, and it gave an immediate impetus to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  incandescent lighting.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Brighter than early dawn's most brilliant dye are blown clear bands of colour through the sky, That swirl and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  sweep and meet, To break and foam like rainbow veils upon a bubble's dome.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The definition of my experience is difficult. Broadly speaking, it is everything that is connected with what I\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  am experiencing now by certain links, of which the various forms of memory are among the most important.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  And so, if I had been delayed by a quarter of an hour or even less, the frigate would have gone without me, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  I would have missed out on this unearthly, extraordinary, and inconceivable expedition, whose true story might\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  well meet with some scepticism.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The uncouth faces passed him two by two, stained yellow or red, or livid by the sea, and as he strove to look at\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  them with ease and indifference, a faint stain of personal shame and commiseration rose to his own face.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  One of his militia generals suggested that the governor should require the outlaws at Lawrence and elsewhere to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  surrender the Sharps rifles. Another wrote asking him to call out the government troops at Fort Leavenworth,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Like his unfortunate little cousin the teal, he too had felt the fear of death smitten into his heart, and was\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  heading desperately for the refuge of some dark overhanging bank deep fringed with weeds where the dreadful eye\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  of the hawk should not discern him.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  To all appearance, Molly had got through her after dinner work in an exemplary manner, had cleaned herself with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  great despatch, and now came to ask submissively if she should sit down to her spinning till milking time.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  You must know, said Margolot, when they were all seated together on the broad window seat, that my husband\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  foolishly gave away all the powder of life he first made to old Momby the witch, who used to live in the country\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  of the Gillikans, to the north of here.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  It was idle for him to move himself to be generous towards them, to tell himself that if he ever came to their\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  gates, stripped of his pride, beaten and in beggars' weeds, that they would be generous towards him, loving him\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  as themselves.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Well, you know, Rady, women like wicked fellows. It is contrast, I suppose, but they do, and I'm sure, from what\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Bracton has said to me I know him intimately, that Dorcas likes him, and I can't conceive why they are not\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  married.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  It was a look so intelligent, yet inexplicable, perverse, sometimes so malicious, but generally accompanied by a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  wild flow of spirits, that Hester could not help questioning at such moments whether Pearl was a human child.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  He doesn't say exactly what it is, said Ruth, a little dubiously. But it's something about land and railroads,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  and thee knows, father, that fortunes are made nobody knows exactly how, in a new country.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  In the shooting of Sheriff Jones in Lawrence, and in the refusal of ex Governor Reeder to allow the deputy\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  marshal to arrest him, they discovered grave offenses against the territorial and the United States laws\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  I can afford to smile because I am absolutely powerless before you. But I do not the less feel that in a matter\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  of which the progress of the world is concerned, I, or rather we, have been put down by brute force.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Sheriff Jones had his pockets always full of writs issued in the spirit of persecution, but was often baffled by\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[187.88074, "o", "\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  the sharp wits and ready resources of the Free State people, and sometimes defied outright.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  but this inestimable privilege was soon violated with the knowledge of truth, the emperor imbibed the maxims of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  persecution, and the sects which descented from the Catholic Church were afflicted and oppressed by the triumph\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  of Christianity.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The place he had was a very good one. The sun shone on him. As to fresh air there was enough of that, and round\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  him grew many large sized comrades, pines as well as firs.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  We have always thought that it was sometimes a courageous act, and, at least, a simple and useful deed, worthy\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  of the sympathetic attention which duty accepted and fulfilled merits,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  I am a very unpleasant pupil, always asking questions, curious, troublesome, insatiable, and even supposing that\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  I could meet with the teacher I require. I am afraid I am not rich enough to pay him.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  We sometimes have images that are by no means peculiarly vague, which yet we do not trust. For example, under\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  the influence of fatigue, we may see a friend's face vividly and clearly, but horribly distorted,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  They are beyond all other works that I know existing, dependent for their effect on low, subdued tones, their\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  favourite choice in time of day being either dawn or twilight, and even their brightest sunsets produced chiefly\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  out of grey paper.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  thinks I o' myself, I never seen anything Osh Popum couldn't mend if he took time enough and glue enough. So I\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  carried this little feller home in a bushel basket one night last month, and I've spent eleven evenings putting\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  him together.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Nothing will be more precious to you, I think, in the practical study of art, than the conviction, which will\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  force itself on you more and more every hour, of the way all things are bound together, little and great, in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  spirit and in matter.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  With many variations, suggested by the nature of his building materials, diversity of climate, and a different\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  mode of social life, Governor Bellingham had planned his new habitation after the residences of gentlemen of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  fair estate in his native land.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  At last the little mice stayed away also, and the tree sighed. After all, it was very pleasant when the sleek\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  little mice sat round me and listened to what I told them.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  They were later used as reserve machines and finally, with the engine, retired from service as part of the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  collection of Edisonia. But they remain in practically as good condition as when installed in eighteen eighty\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  three.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Now, this knife was a splendid one, though half the blade was gone, and the handle was a little cracked, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Anders knew that one is almost a man as soon as one has a jackknife.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  But they dragged him out of the room and up the stairs into the loft, and here, in a dark corner, where no\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  daylight could enter, they left him.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  In the supposed depths of this dialogue, the Neoplatonists found hidden meanings and connections with the Jewish\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  and Christian scriptures, and out of them they elicited doctrines quite at variance with the spirit of Plato.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The modest fellow would have liked fame thrust upon him for some worthy achievement. It might be for a book, or\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  for the skilful management of some great newspaper, or for some daring expedition like that of Lieutenant Strain\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  or Doctor Kane.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  That would be very well, my child, replied her father, if your plan were not liable to be frustrated by ordinary\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  cunning. But no doubt this image had been already missed by its owner, and he will have set it down for certain\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  that it was taken out of the room by the person he locked up there.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  one perceives, without understanding it, a hideous murmur, sounding almost like human accents, but more nearly\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  resembling a howl than an articulate word.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  mister Meadowcroft the elder, having not spoken one word thus far, himself introduced the newcomer to me, with a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  side glance at his sons, which had something like defiance in it, a glance which, as I was sorry to notice, was\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  returned with the defiance on their side by the two young men.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Now for one little half hour she had been a woman talking to a boy. No, not even that. She had been talking,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  just talking. There were no persons in the conversation, just things one thing cotton.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  We do not know how Plato would have arranged his own dialogues, or whether the thought of arranging any of them,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  besides the two trilogies which he has expressly connected, was ever present to his mind.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  for it is a solid, heavy, handsome door, and must once have been in the habit of shutting with a sonorous bang\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  behind the liveried lackey, who had just seen his master and mistress off the grounds, in a carriage and pair.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[187.880784, "o", "\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  You will carry out with you one hundred men of the North Northwest Birmingham regiment, which will probably\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  suffice for your own security, as it is thought that if mister Neverben be withdrawn, the people will revert\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  easily to their old habits of obedience.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  It was strange, too, that he found an arid pleasure in following up to the end the rigid lines of the doctrines\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  of the Church, and penetrating into obscure silences only to hear and feel the more deeply his own condemnation.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The fancies of the Neoplatonists are only interesting to us because they exhibit a phase of the human mind which\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  prevailed widely in the first centuries of the Christian era, and is not wholly extinct in our own day.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  It is to let Hamlet, if that happened to be the name of your character, enter with a small dog, pet falcon,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  mongoose, tame bear, or whatever animal is most in keeping with the part, and confide in this animal such\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  sorrows, hopes, or secret history as the audience has got to know.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The face of the mahogany shone with delight, and why not, when it was doing everything, almost everything,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  within the scope of a piano, and yet the family had enjoyed weeks of good, nourishing meals on what had been\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  saved by its exertions.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Eleven o'clock had struck. It was a fine, clear night, there were the only persons on the road, and they\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  sauntered leisurely along, to avoid paying the price of fatigue for the recreation provided for the Toledans in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  the valley or on the banks of their river.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  There is a want of flow, and often a defect of rhythm. The meaning is sometimes obscure, and there is a greater\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  use of apposition and more of repetition than occurs in Plato's earlier writings.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  but when it came to be a question of lighting a scattered suburb, a group of dwellings on the outskirts, a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  remote country residence, or a farmhouse, the alternating current, in all elements, save its danger, was and is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  ideal.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Habit is a concept involving the occurrence of similar events at different times. If the behaviorist feels\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  confident that there is such a phenomenon as habit, that can only be because he trusts his memory, when it\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  assures him that there have been other times.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  A few years back one of their slaves, a coachman, was kept on the coach box one cold night when they were out at\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  a ball until he became almost frozen to death. In fact, he did die in the infirmary from the effects of the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  frost about one week afterwards.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  My pursuits are peaceful, and my temper, I humbly trust, is greatly given to mercy and love, returned David, a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  little nettled at so direct an attack on his manhood. But there are none who can say that I have ever forgotten\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  my faith in the Lord, even in the greatest straits.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  If it be granted, first, that the thoughts of a certain character should be known to the audience, and secondly,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  that soliloquy, or the habit of thinking aloud, is in opposition to modern stage type think, how shall a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  soliloquy be avoided without damage to the play?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  we shall be blown up but no the dazzling disk of mysterious light nimbly leaps aside. It approaches Hans, who\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  fixes his blue eye upon it steadily. It threatens the head of my uncle, who falls upon his knees with his head\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  down to avoid it,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  It was quite true that a vessel was in sight, hardly more than six miles from the shore, but owing to the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  increase in the earth's convexity and the consequent limitation of the range of vision, the rigging of the top\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  masts alone was visible above the water.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The departing ladies who had said they would stay didn't, of course, thank heaven, stay, they departed, in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  consequence of arrangements made. In a rage of curiosity, as they professed, produced by the touches with which\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  he had already worked us up.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  By degrees all his happiness, all his brilliancy, subsided into regret and uneasiness, so that his limbs lost\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  their power, his arms hung heavily by his sides, and his head drooped as though he was stupefied.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The law of that school is that everything shall be seen clearly, or at least only in such mist or faintness as\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  shall be delightful, and I have no doubt that the best introduction to it would be the elementary practice of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  painting every study on a golden ground.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Toddy, however, had descended from her chair with great swiftness, and was already in retreat towards the dairy,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  with a sort of waddling run, and an amount of fat on the nape of her neck, which made her look like the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  metamorphosis of a white suckling pig.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  At that epoch of pristine simplicity, however, matters of even slighter public interest, and of far less\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  intrinsic weight than the welfare of Hester and her child were strangely mixed up with the deliberations of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  legislators and acts of state.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The condition is that I will be permitted to make Luther talk American, streamline him, so to speak, because you\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  will never get people, whether in or outside the Lutheran Church, actually to read Luther unless we make him\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  talk as he would talk to day to Americans.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The family likeness between her and her niece Dinah Morris, with a contrast between her keenness and Dinah's\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  seraphic gentleness of expression, might have served a painter as an excellent suggestion for Amartha and Mary.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  When I found it I said to myself that it would do nicely for my servant girl, for when she was brought to life\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  she would not be proud nor haughty, as the glass cat is, for such a dreadful mixture of colours would discourage\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  her from trying to be as dignified as the blue munchkins are.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Brooding over all these matters, the mother felt like one who has evoked a spirit, but, by some irregularity in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  the process of conjuration, has failed to win the master word that should control this new and incomprehensible\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  intelligence.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  This, I felt, was paid to me as being President of the Republic, and I endeavoured to behave myself with such\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  mingled humility and dignity as might befit the occasion. But I could not but feel that something was wanting to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  the simplicity of my ordinary life.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Do not suppose, however, that Mrs. Poyser was elderly or shrewish in her appearance. She was a good looking\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  woman, not more than eight and thirty, of fair complexion and sandy hair, well shapen, light footed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  There were a few rose bushes, however, and a number of apple trees, probably the descendants of those planted by\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  the Reverend mister Blackstone, the first settler of the peninsula, that half mythological personage who rides\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  through our early annals seated on the back of a bull.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The description she gave of the coming reception to the Women's Political League was so humorous and diverting\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  that they were both laughing heartily over the thing when the young people passed them, and thus mister Hopkins\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  failed to notice who the occupants of the other vehicle were.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  My heart doth plead that thou in him dost lie, A closet never pierced with crystal eyes. But the defendant doth\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  that plea deny, And says in him thy fair appearance lies.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Idle and embittering finally to argue against his own dispassionate certitude that the commandment of love bade\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  us not to love our neighbour as ourselves with the same amount and intensity of love, but to love him as\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  ourselves with the same kind of love.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Of what Mrs. Neverben had gone through in providing birds, beasts, and fishes, not to talk of tarts and jellies\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  for the dinner of that day, no one but myself can have any idea, but it must be admitted that she accomplished\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  her task with thorough success.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Indeed, irresolution being the keynote of Hamlet's soliloquy, a clever player could to some extent indicate the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  whole thirty lines by a silent working of the jaw, but at the same time it would be idle to deny that he would\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  miss the finer shades of the dramatist's meaning,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Her face was an enigma, for it inspired everyone with the warmest sympathy, and yet, if you examined it\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  attentively, there was not one beautiful feature. She could not be called handsome, but no one could have\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  thought her ugly.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Whether or not this principle is liable to exceptions, every one would agree that it has a broad measure of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  truth, though the word exactly might seem an overstatement, and it might seem more correct to say that ideas\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  approximately represent impressions.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  It was further decorated with strange and seemingly cabalistic figures and diagrams, suitable to the quaint\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  taste of the age which had been drawn in the stucco when newly laid on, and had now grown hard and durable for\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  the admiration of after times.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The guards had a terrible struggle with the goat, which was loose in the room, and still wanted to fight, but\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  finally they subdued the animal, and then they took the boolaroo out of the frame he was tied in, and brought\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  both him and the goat before Queen Trot, who awaited them in the throne room of the palace.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  This attitude springs from a false conception of sin, the conception that sin is a small matter, easily taken\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  care of by good works, that we must present ourselves unto God with a good conscience, that we must feel no sin\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[187.880842, "o", "\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  before we may feel that Christ was given for our sins.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The mergantzer had a crested head of iridescent green black, a broad collar of lustrous white, black back, black\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  and white wings, white belly, sides finely penciled in black and white, and a breast of rich chestnut red\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  streaked with black.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Associated with this simple form of apparatus were various ingenious details and refinements to secure\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  regularity of operation, freedom from inaccuracy, and immunity from such tampering as would permit theft of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  current or damage.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  This at once compels you to understand that the work is to be imaginative and decorative, that it represents\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[187.880864, "o", "\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  beautiful things, in the clearest way, but not under existing conditions, and that, in fact, you are producing\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  jeweller's work rather than pictures.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Hester could only account for the child's character, and even then most vaguely and imperfectly, by recalling\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  what she herself had been during that momentous period, while Pearl was imbibing her soul from the spiritual\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  world and her bodily frame from its material of earth.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  And she took Ander's hand and walked with him up the broad marble stairs, where soldiers were posted at every\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  third step, and through the magnificent halls, where courtiers in silk and velvet stood bowing wherever he went.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The practice of gathering its proselytes into one place prevents the building up and strengthening of foreign\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  branches, and inasmuch as extensive and strong organizations are seldom met with abroad, very erroneous ideas\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  exist concerning the strength of the church.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  There are, however, several points in which such an account of recognition is inadequate. To begin with, it\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  might seem at first sight more correct to define recognition as I have seen this before than as this has existed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  before.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  God, as a direct consequence of the sin which man thus punished, had given her a lovely child, whose place was\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  on that same dishonored bosom to connect her parent for ever with the race and descent of mortals, and to be\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  finally a blessed soul in heaven.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  In place of a single hamlet, in the smallest corner of which the members could have congregated, there now are\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  about seventy stakes of Zion and about seven hundred organized wards, each ward and stake with its full\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  complement of officers and priesthood organizations.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  On the table, in token that the sentiment of old English hospitality had not been left behind, stood a large\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  pewter tankard, at the bottom of which, had Hester or Pearl peeped into it, they might have seen the frothy\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  remnant of a recent draught of ale.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  P.S. Pray, sir, excuse me for writing to you a second time. I could not help writing, partly to tell you how\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  thankful I am for your kindness, and partly to let you know that your advice shall not be wasted, however\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  sorrowfully and reluctantly it may be at first followed. CB\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  But the actual course of development has been somewhat different from this ideal scheme. Leisure held the first\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  place at the start and came to hold a rank very much above wasteful consumption of goods, both as a direct\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  exponent of wealth and as an element in the standard of decency during the quasi peaceable culture.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The dynamo electric machine, though small, was robust, for under all the varying speeds of water power and the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  vicissitudes of the plant to which it belonged, it continued in active use until eighteen ninety nine, seventeen\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  years.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  If a man had stolen a pound in his youth and had used that pound to amass a huge fortune, how much was he\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  obliged to give back? The pound he had stolen only, or the pound together with the compound interest accruing\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  upon it, or all his huge fortune?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  But, continued Raoul, not interrupted by this movement of his friend, heaven be praised, the French, who are\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  pronounced to be thoughtless and indiscreet, reckless even, are capable of bringing a calm and sound judgment to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  bear on matters of such high importance.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Our confidence or lack of confidence in the accuracy of a memory image must, in fundamental cases, be based upon\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  a characteristic of the image itself, since we cannot evoke the past bodily and compare it with the present\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  image.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The net and web of endless things had been crawling and creeping around her. She had struggled in dumb,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  speechless terror against some mighty grasping that strove for her life, with gnarled and creeping fingers, but\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  now at last, weakly, she opened her eyes and questioned.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  This nobleman's character, though celebrated for political courage and conduct, was very low for military\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  prowess, and after some skirmishes in which he was worsted, he here allowed Montrose to escape him.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Coming by way of the Missouri River towns, he fell first among border ruffian companionship and influences, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  perhaps having his inclinations already moulded by his Washington instructions, his early impressions were\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  decidedly adverse to the Free State cause.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Harry was placed in the custody of Captain Martin of the Kickapoo Rangers, who proved a kind jailer, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  materially assisted in protecting him from the dangerous intentions of the mob which at that time held\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Leavenworth under the reign of terror.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Nor was Rodolfo less surprised than they, and the better to assure himself of so wonderful a fact, he begged\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Leucadia to give him some token which should make perfectly clear to him that which indeed he did not doubt,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  since it was authenticated by his parents.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The Book of Mormon had taught the people the true origin and destiny of the American Indians, and toward this\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  dark skinned remnant of a once mighty people, the missionaries of Mormonism early turned their eyes, and with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  their eyes went their hearts and their hopes.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Can one imagine a naturalist refusing to study the viper, the bat, the scorpion, the centipede, the tarantula,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  and one who would cast them back into their darkness saying, Oh, how ugly that is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  No matter then, although my foot did stand, Upon the farthest earth, removed from thee, For nimble thought can\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  jump both sea and land, As soon as think the place where he would be. But ah,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  They were absorbed in his theology and were under the dominion of his name, while that which was truly great and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  truly characteristic in him, his effort to realize and connect abstractions, was not understood by them at all.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  What is called perception differs from sensation by the fact that the sensational ingredients bring up habitual\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  associates, images and expectations of their usual correlates, all of which are subjectively indistinguishable\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  from the sensation.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  You are my all the world, and I must strive To know my shames and praises from your tongue, None else to me, nor\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  I to none alive, That my steeled sense or changes right or wrong.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Although only a moderate breeze was blowing, the sea was rough, a circumstance to be accounted for only by the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  diminution in the force of the earth's attraction, rendering the liquid particles so buoyant, that by the mere\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  effect of oscillation they were carried to a height that was quite unprecedented.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  For God's sake, my lady mother, give me a wife who would be an agreeable companion, not one who will disgust me,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  so that we may both bear evenly and with mutual good will the yoke imposed on us by heaven, instead of pulling\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  this way and that way and fretting each other to death.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  I heard a noise behind. I turned and saw Kafir, his black eyes shining, while in his hand he held a gleaming\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  knife. He lifted it above his head as if to strike, but I had the strength of ten men, and I hurled him from me.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  She reflected how near she stood to the crisis which was to determine whether she was to be blessed or unhappy\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  for ever, and racked by the intensity of her emotions, she suddenly changed colour, her head dropped, and she\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  fell forward in a swoon into the arms of the dismayed Estefania.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  A slight diminution in the excessively high temperature which had prevailed for the last few weeks was the only\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  apparent change in the general order of things. But whether this was to be attributed to any alteration in the\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[187.880931, "o", "\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Earth's orbit was a question which would still require several days to decide.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The arc lamp, installed outside a customer's premises, or in a circuit for public street lighting, burned so\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  many hours nightly, so many nights in the month, and was paid for at that rate, subject to rebate for hours when\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  the lamp might be out through accident.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  In December eighteen eighty eight, mister W. J. Jenks read an interesting paper before the American Institute of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Electrical Engineers on the six years of practical experience had up to that time with the meter, then more\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  generally in use than any other.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  For many, then, this book has been a source of fascination, surely one of the most influential novels ever\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  written, an inspiration for such scientists and discoverers as engineer Simon Lake, oceanographer William B.B.,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  polar traveller Sir Ernest Shackleton.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[187.880958, "o", "\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  those pretty wrongs that liberty commits, When I am some time absent from thy heart, Thy beauty and thy years\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  full well befits, For still temptation follows where thou art.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Though thrown into prison for this enterprise and detained some time, he was not discouraged, but still\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  continued by his countenance and protection to infuse spirit into the distressed royalists.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  They began with the one in the family sitting room Colonel Wheeler, Ralph Thurston, mister and Mrs Bill Harmon\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  with Natty and Ruffus, mister and Mrs. Popham with Digby and Lally Joy, all standing in admiring groups and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  thrilling with delight at the order of events.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  It was through Floyd's advice that Buchanan ordered the military expedition to Utah, ostensibly to install\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  certain federal officials and to repress an alleged infantile rebellion, which in fact had never come into\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  existence, but in reality to further the interests of the secessionists.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Historians at least, perhaps from their own ignorance and inexperience, have not remarked anything but a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  headlong, impetuous conduct, each party hurrying to a battle, where valour and fortune chiefly determine the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  success,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  They knew no north, no south, no east, no west. They stood positively by the Constitution, and would have\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  nothing to do in the bloody strife between brothers, unless indeed they were summoned by the authority to which\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  they had already once loyally responded, to furnish men in arms for the country's need.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Besides members of Parliament who were excluded, many officers, unwilling to serve under the new generals, threw\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  up their commissions and unwarily facilitated the project of putting the army entirely into the hands of that\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  faction.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The mother, as soon as the chase is so far turned that Mary can no longer watch the expression of her\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  countenance, goes away from the door with a smile of complacency and satisfaction on her face at the ingenuity\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  and success of her little artifice.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  By being studious of colour they are studious of division, and while the curoscurist devotes himself to the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  representation of degrees of force in one thing, unseparated light, the colourists have for their function the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  attainment of beauty by arrangement of the divisions of light.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Ho, ye sails that seem to wander in dream filled meadows, say, is the shore where I stand the only field of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  struggle, or are ye hit and battered out there by waves and wind gusts as ye tack over a clashing sea of watery\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  echoes?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Everyone could observe his agitation and prostration, a prostration which was, indeed, the more remarkable since\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  people were not accustomed to see him, with his arms hanging listlessly by his side, his head bewildered, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  his eyes with all their bright intelligence bedimmed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  I see a quantity of chairs for hire at the rate of one soux, men reading the newspaper under the shade of the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  trees, girls and men breakfasting either alone or in company, waiters who were rapidly going up and down a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  narrow staircase hidden under the foliage.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Had Eva Cressweller not been good looking? Had Jack been still at college? Had Sir Kennington Oval remained in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  England? Had mister Bunnet and the barkeeper not succeeded in stopping my carriage on the hill? Should I have\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  succeeded in arranging for the final departure of my old friend?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  It would seem that only rather recent events can be placed at all accurately by means of feelings giving their\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  temporal relation to the present, but it is clear that such feelings must play an essential part in the process\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  of dating remembered events.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Then, heaving a heavy sigh, probably among the last he ever drew in pining for a condition he had so long\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  abandoned, he added, It is what I would wish to practice myself, as one without a cross of blood, though it is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  not always easy to deal with an Indian as you would with a fellow Christian.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  You will forgive me, dear reader, if I have made you attend the funeral of Sylvia ten years before her death.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Believe me, I have no intention of performing a miracle. You may console yourself with the idea that I shall\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  spare you that unpleasant task when poor Sylvia dies.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  For instance, one day the children had been playing upon the piazza with blocks and other playthings, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  finally had gone into the house, leaving all the things on the floor of the piazza, instead of putting them away\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  in their places, as they ought to have done.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Come, come, returned Hawkeye, uncasing his honest countenance, the better to assure the wavering confidence of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  his companion. You may see a skin which, if it be not as white as one of the gentle ones, has no tinge of red to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  it that the winds of the heaven and the sun have not bestowed. Now let us to business.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Sylvia was the adoration of France, and her talent was the real support of all the comedies which the greatest\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  authors wrote for her, especially of the plays of Marivaux, for without her his comedies would never have gone\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  to posterity.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  It will be well for you, if you join not with those who instead of kites fly falcons, who instead of obeying the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  last words of the great cloud shepherd, to feed his sheep, live the lives. How much less than vanity of the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  werewolf and the gear eagle?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  All dissent, all noncompliance, all hesitation, all mere silence even, were in their stronghold towns, like\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Leavenworth, branded as abolitionism, declared to be hostility to the public welfare, and punished with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  proscription, personal violence, expulsion, and frequently death.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The period was hardly, if at all, earlier than that of our story, when a dispute concerning the right of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  property in a pig not only caused a fierce and bitter contest in the legislative body of the colony, but\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  resulted in an important modification of the framework itself of the legislature.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  If any still retained rancor against him in his present condition, they passed in silence, while his well\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  wishers, more generous than prudent, accompanied his march with tears, with acclamations and with prayers for\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  his safety.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Thus, if I recognize a thing, the occasion of its previous existence, in virtue of which I recognize it, forms\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  part of my experience, by definition. Recognition will be one of the marks by which my experience is singled out\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  from the rest of the world.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Envy, hatred, malice, and uncharitableness are never so essentially detestable to my mind as when they "]
[187.880968, "o", "are\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  animated by the sense of propriety and work under the surface. But for my interest in Naomi and my other\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  interest in the little love looks which I now and then surprised passing between her and Ambrose, I should never\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  have sat through that supper.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Let a man run, and everybody will run after him. The crowd will not stop unless the man is proved to be mad. But\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  to prove it is indeed a difficult task, because we have a crowd of men who, mad from their birth, are still\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  considered wise.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  However, remembering what you told me, namely that you had commended the matter to a higher decision than ours,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  and that you were resolved to submit with resignation to that decision, whatever it might be, I hold it my duty\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  to yield also and to be silent, and may be all for the best.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The axe struck deep into the very pith. The tree fell to the earth with a sigh. He felt a pang. It was like a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  swoon. He could not think of happiness, for he was sorrowful at being separated from his home from the place\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  where he had sprung up.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Well then, last, here is Turner's, Greek school of the highest class, and you define his art absolutely, as\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  first the displaying intensely and with the sternest intellect, of natural form as it is, and then the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  envelopment of it with cloud and fire.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  With a further advance in culture, this taboo may change into simple custom of a more or less rigorous\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  character, but whatever be the theoretical basis of the distinction which is maintained, whether it be a taboo\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[187.881034, "o", "\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  or a larger conventionality, the features of the conventional scheme of consumption do not change easily.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  All the territorial dignitaries were present. Governor Shannon presided, John Calhoun, the Surveyor General,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  made the principal speech, a denunciation of the abolitionists supporting the Topeka movement. Chief Justice\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Lecomte dignified the occasion with approving remarks.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  We have spoken of Pearl's rich and luxuriant beauty, a beauty that shone with deep and vivid tints, a bright\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  complexion, eyes possessing intensity both of depth and glow, and hair already of a deep glossy brown, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  which, in after years, would be nearly akin to black.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  At the conclusion of the banquet, which was served at five o'clock, the king entered his cabinet, where his\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  tailors were awaiting him for the purpose of trying on the celebrated costume representing spring, which was the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  result of so much imagination, and had cost so many efforts of thought to the designers and ornament workers of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  the court.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Nevertheless, the mustard seed, among the smallest of all seeds, has attained the proportions of a tree, and the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  birds of the air are nesting in its branches. The acorn is now an oak, offering protection and the sweets of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  satisfaction to every earnest pilgrim journeying its way for truth.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  It will be observed that an organized mob, aided by many of the civil and military officers of Missouri, with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Governor Boggs at their head, have been the prominent actors in this business, incited, too, it appears, against\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  the Mormons by political hatred, and by the additional motives of plunder and revenge.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  They look something alike, you know, suggested the captain of the guards, looking from one to the other\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  doubtfully. And they're nearly the same size if you stand the goat on his hind legs. They've both got the same\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  style of whiskers, and they're both of them obstinate and dangerous, so they ought to make a good patch.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Splendid\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  For general service, therefore, requiring no special effort, the numerical strength of the factions was about\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  equal, while on extraordinary occasions the two thousand border ruffian reserve lying a little farther back from\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  the state line could at any time easily turn the scale.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  But neither Saint Gerard, nor Broad Street, neither wonders of the Mint, nor the glories of the hall, where the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  ghosts of our fathers sit always signing the Declaration, impressed the visitors so much as the splendours of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  the Chestnut Street windows and the bargains on Eighth Street.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Montrose, weak in cavalry, here lined his troops of horse with infantry, and after putting the enemy's horse to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  rout, fell with united force upon their foot, who were entirely cut in pieces, though with the loss of the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  gallant Lord Gordon on the part of the Royalists.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  It has been my privilege to tread the soil of many lands, to observe the customs and study the habits of more\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  nations than one, and I have yet to find the place and meet the people, where and with whom the purity of man\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  and woman is held more precious than among the maligned Mormons in the mountain valleys of the west.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Owing to his insistence on low pressure, direct current for use in densely populated districts as the only safe\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  and truly universal, profitable way of delivering electrical energy to the consumers, Edison has been frequently\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  spoken of as an opponent of the alternating current.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Edison had installed his historic first great central station system in New York on the multiple arc system\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  covered by his feeder and main invention, which resulted in a notable saving in the cost of conductors, as\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  against a straight two wire system throughout of the tree kind.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  In the early morning of the next day, May twenty ninth, a company of dragoons with one empty saddle came down\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  from the fort, and while the pro slavery men still slept, the prisoner and his escort were on their way across\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  the prairies to Lecompton in the charge of officers of the United States Army,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  thou gentle maid of silent valleys and of modest brooks, for thou shalt be clothed in light, and fed with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  morning manna, Till summer's heat melts thee beside the fountains and the springs, To flourish in eternal vales.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  They, why should thou complain?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  And therefore to you I turn, Timaeus, citizen of Locris, who are at once a philosopher and a statesman, and to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  you, Critias, whom all Athenians know to be similarly accomplished, and to Hermocrates, who is also fitted by\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  nature and education, to share in our discourse.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  This compulsion leads Nemo into ugly contradictions. He is a fighter for freedom, yet all who board his ship are\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  imprisoned there for good. He works to save lives, both human and animal, yet he himself creates a holocaust. He\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  detests imperialism, yet he lays personal claim to the South Pole.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Their piety would be like their names, like their faces, like their clothes, and it was idle for him to tell\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  himself that their humble and contrite hearts it might be, paid a far richer tribute of devotion than his had\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  ever been, a gift tenfold more acceptable than his elaborate adoration.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Then again there was no known way to lubricate an engine for continuous running, and mister Edison informed me\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  that, as a marine engine started before the ship left New York and continued running until it reached its home\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  port, so an engine for his purposes must produce light at all times.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The man of the household also can do something in this direction, and indeed he commonly does, but with a still\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  lower descent into the levels of indigence along the margin of the slums, the man and presently also the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  children virtually cease to consume valuable goods for appearances, and the woman remains virtually the sole\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  exponent of the household's pecuniary decency.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Angry with himself, he tried to hide his face from their eyes by gazing down sideways into the shallow, swirling\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  water under the bridge, but he still saw a reflection therein of their top heavy silk hats, and humble tape like\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  collars, and loosely hanging clerical clothes. Brother Hickey\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Here is an equally typical Greek school landscape by Wilson, lost wholly in golden mist, the trees so slightly\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  drawn that you don't know if they are trees or towers, and no care for colour whatsoever. Perfectly deceptive\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  and marvelous effect of sunshine through the mist Apollo and the python.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Constantine easily believed that the heretics, who presumed to dispute his opinions, or to oppose his commands,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  were guilty of the most absurd and criminal obstinacy, and that a seasonable application of moderate severities\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  might save those unhappy men from the danger of an everlasting condemnation.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  When the music, by its bursts of melody, carried away these illustrious dancers, when the simple, untutored\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  pantomime of that period, only the more natural on account of the very indifferent acting of the august actors,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  had reached its culminating point of triumph, the theatre shook with tumultuous applause.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The Free State men had only their convictions, their intelligence, their courage, and the moral support of the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  North. The conspiracy had its secret combination, the territorial officials, the legislature, the bogus laws,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  the courts, the militia officers, the President, and the army,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  In determining whether two or more allied forms ought to be ranked as species or varieties, naturalists are\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  practically guided by the following considerations, namely, the amount of difference between them, and whether\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  such differences relate to few or many points of structure, and whether they are of physiological importance,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  but more especially whether they are constant.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  I can no more help spending my life in trying to do what I can for the souls of others, than you could help\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  running if you heard little Toddy crying at the other end of the house. The voice would go to your heart, you\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  would think the dear child was in trouble or in danger, and you couldn't rest without running to help her and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  comfort her.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The Free State Hotel, a stone building in dimensions fifty by seventy feet, three stories high and handsomely\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[187.881041, "o", "\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  furnished, previously occupied only for lodging rooms, on that day for the first time opened its table\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  accommodations to the public and provided a free dinner in honour of the occasion.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The Scottish generals and commissioners effected great surprise on the appearance of the king, and though they\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  paid him all the exterior respect due to his dignity, they instantly set a guard upon him under colour of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  protection, and made him in reality a prisoner.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The present chapters can only touch upon the more salient movements of the Civil War in Kansas, which, happily,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  are not sanguinary. If, however, the individual and more isolated cases of bloodshed could be described, they\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  would show a startling aggregate of barbarity and a loss of life for opinion's sake.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[187.881089, "o", "\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  He had a good appetite, could tell a good story without laughing, was celebrated for his witty repartes and his\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  sociable manners, but he spent his life at home, seldom going out and seeing hardly any one, because he always\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  had a pipe in his mouth and was surrounded by at least twenty cats with which he would amuse himself all day.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  But he has not as yet defined this intermediate territory which lies somewhere between medicine and mathematics,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  and he would have felt that there was as great an impiety in ranking theories of physics first in the order of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  knowledge as in placing the body before the soul.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Recognition in this sense does not necessarily involve more than a habit of association. The kind of object we\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  are seeing at the moment is associated with the word cat, or with an auditory image of purring, or whatever\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  other characteristic we may happen to recognize in the cat of the moment.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The mother herself, as if the red ignominy were so deeply scorched into her brain that all her conceptions\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  assumed its form, had carefully wrought out the similitude, lavishing many hours of morbid ingenuity to create\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  an analogy between the object of her affection and the emblem of her guilt and torture,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  I love thee with a love I seemed to lose with my lost saints. I love thee with the breath, smiles, tears of all\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  my life, and, if God choose, I shall but love thee better after death.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  And the men of Israel answered the men of Judah and said, We have ten parts in the king, and we have also more\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  right in David than ye. Why then did ye despise us, that our advice should not be first had in bringing back our\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  king?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  It seems to me, I replied, that such approval, such ratification of the opinion expressed by the king, the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  princes of the blood, etc., is rather a proof of the affection felt for them by the nation, for the French carry\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  that affection to such an extent that they believe them infallible.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  For, believe me, the final philosophy of art can only ratify their opinion that the beauty of a cock robin is to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  be red, and of a grass plot to be green, and the best skill of art is in instantly seizing on the manifold\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  deliciousness of light, which you can only seize by precision of instantaneous touch.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Guided by you, how we might stroll towards death, our only music one another's breath, Through gardens intimate\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  with hollyhocks, where silent poppies burn between the rocks, By pools where birches bend to confidants above\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  green waters scummed with lily plants.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  The mystery of their origin, their capacity for evolving latent faculties of crime, and the steady vitality with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  which they survive the hearse and speak their deep mouthed malignities in every newborn generation, have\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  associated them somehow in my mind with a spell of life exceeding and distinct from human and a special satanic\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  action.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  With Heraclitus he acknowledges the perpetual flux. Like Anaxagoras, he asserts the predominance of mind,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  although admitting an element of necessity which reason is incapable of subduing. Like the Pythagoreans, he\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  supposes the mystery of the world to be contained in number.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Exquisite order and universal, with eternal life and light, this is the faith and effort of the schools of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  crystal, and you may describe and complete their work quite literally, by taking any verses of Chaucer in his\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  tender mood, and observing how he insists on the clearness and brightness first, and then on the order.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  With these and some reinforcements of the Athol men and Macdonald's whom he had recalled, Montrose fell suddenly\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  upon Argyll's country, and let loose upon it all the rage of war, carrying off the cattle, burning the houses,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  and putting the inhabitants to the sword.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  After an apprenticeship on a merchant ship he had entered the Imperial Navy, and had already reached the rank of\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  lieutenant when the Count appointed him to the charge of his own private yacht, in which he was accustomed to\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  spend by far the greater part of his time, throughout the winter generally cruising in the Mediterranean, whilst\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  in the summer he visited more northern waters.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Even the supporting cast is shrewdly drawn. Professor Arenax, the career scientist caught in an ethical\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  conflict, Conseil, the compulsive classifier, who supplies humorous taglines for Verne's fast facts. The\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  harpooner Ned Land, a creature of constant appetites, man as heroic animal.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  From the undersurface of the clouds there are continual emissions of lurid light. Electric matter is in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  continual evolution from their component molecules. The gaseous elements of the air need to be slaked with\u001b[0m"]
[187.881119, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  moisture, for innumerable columns of water rush upwards into the air and fall back again in white foam.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Five hundred men more, who had been levied by the Covenanters, were persuaded to embrace the royal cause, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  with this combined force he hastened to attack Lord Elko, who lay at Perth with an army of six thousand men,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  assembled upon the first news of the Irish invasion.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  Beholding it, Hester was constrained to rush towards the child, to pursue the little elf in the flight which she\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  invariably began, to snatch her to her bosom with a close pressure and earnest kisses, not so much from\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2K\u001b[2m  overflowing love as to assure herself that Pearl was flesh and blood and not utterly delusive.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
